---
import RevealText from './RevealText.astro';
---

<section class="project-meaning" id="what-is-zerocloud" aria-labelledby="meaning-title">
  <div class="meaning-lead">
    <h2 class="meaning-title" id="meaning-title" data-enter>
      <span class="meaning-zero" aria-hidden="true">0</span>
      <span class="visually-hidden">Zero </span>
      <span class="meaning-words"><RevealText text="required cloud services." /></span>
    </h2>
    <p class="meaning-intro" data-enter>
      That’s what the zero in ZeroCloud stands for. An app’s main job should keep working on
      hardware you own, even if your internet connection drops or a service shuts down.
    </p>
  </div>
  <dl class="meaning-index">
    <div>
      <dt data-enter><RevealText text="On your device" /></dt>
      <dd>
        Your device runs the app and keeps the working copy of your data. Opening it should never
        depend on signing in to a hosted account.
      </dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt data-enter><RevealText text="Between your devices" /></dt>
      <dd>
        Choose where a file goes, which devices keep a collection, or where a screen appears. A
        reachable local connection is one way for your devices to work together.
      </dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt data-enter><RevealText text="Online by choice" /></dt>
      <dd>
        Go online for a download, an update, or a guide. Once an app is installed, those services
        should be optional for its everyday use.
      </dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
</section>
